virglrenderer: shader array indexes the guest computes are clamped

What: vrend's TGSI-to-GLSL translator emits array indexes computed at run time
(address registers) as clamp(addrN + offset, 0, size - 1) for uniform block
contents and arrays of blocks, the uniform store (const0), sampler and image
arrays, and temporary arrays. Constant indexes past an array already fail to
compile (GLSL compile-time error, the draws are skipped).
Why: GLSL leaves an index past an array undefined, and the guest's shader picks
it. Apple's GPU then reads or writes outside the array's memory: past a
uniform buffer (virgl-uniform-buffer-checks.patch only guarantees the declared
block size), past the uniform store, past the sampler descriptors, or outside
private memory, any of which can make it fault (a GPU fault resets the GPU; on
2026-10-04 that panicked macOS). WebGL implementations clamp the same way
(ANGLE's SH_CLAMP_INDIRECT_ARRAY_BOUNDS). Varying and output arrays (GPU
registers) and SSBOs (not on macOS' GL 4.1) are left as they are.
Upstream: upstreamable hardening; not sent.
Tests: Tests/virgl/test-gpu-ranges.c (a shader indexing a uniform block with an
address register: the GLSL holds the clamp, and the draw runs); the fuzzer's
shaders go through it on every input.
--- a/src/vrend/vrend_shader.c
+++ b/src/vrend/vrend_shader.c
@@ -933,8 +933,26 @@
    ctx->sampler_arrays[idx].first = first;
    ctx->sampler_arrays[idx].array_size = last - first + 1;
    return true;
+}
+
+/* "clamp(addrN + offset, 0, size - 1)" for an array index the guest's shader computes.
+ * GLSL leaves an index past an array undefined; Apple's GPU then reads or writes outside
+ * the array's memory (uniform buffers, the uniform store, sampler descriptors, private
+ * memory), which can make it fault. Clamping keeps every access inside the array. */
+static const char *clamped_index(char buf[static 64], int addr, int offset, int size)
+{
+   snprintf(buf, 64, "clamp(addr%d + %d, 0, %d)", addr, offset, size > 1 ? size - 1 : 0);
+   return buf;
 }
 
+static int sampler_array_size(const struct dump_ctx *ctx, int first)
+{
+   for (uint32_t i = 0; i < ctx->num_sampler_arrays; i++)
+      if (ctx->sampler_arrays[i].first == first)
+         return ctx->sampler_arrays[i].array_size;
+   return 1;
+}
